  "body": "Firefox 49 implemented a new extended attribute of the Cache-Control response header - immutable, it has not been standardized yet, see [this post](http://bitsup.blogspot.com/2016/05/cache-control-immutable.html) for the details.\n\nSo here is the conflict: should `fetch(aURLWithImmutableCache, {cache: \"no-cache\"})` send a conditional request first or use the cache directly without sending any request? Currently Firefox's behavior is the latter.\n",
